Z||000007||Seanh||12-28-2000||11:41 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/boatr502/leather3.jpg"> <P>Those look great! FieroMaster88, they are fairly easy to install. Mr. Mikes includes a video and all the equipment needed to install them. I am going to order mine this week with my X-Mas money, but they wont be installed for a while.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Black88GT||12-28-2000||12:22 PM||||Sean, let me give you a word of advice, save all the money you can for your engine swap you say you are going to do in January.  Use that 400 - 500 bucks for replacement parts like water pump, oil pump, etc. etc.  I can tell you that things will pop up and if you don't have the cash for it then the car will sit some more.<P>I have always love the leather seats but I am waiting until my car is fast before I do the interior. <P><BR>IMHO<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 12-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||SloPonti||12-28-2000||05:40 PM||||Yes these seats are very very easy to install!! Yes orief i did mention that i did replace the 3.5 in the seat but i do not like the look of the punched holes in the seat! as you can see in the first picture i had furry seat covers on the seat and i could still here my stock headrest speakers just fine! So i talked to Mr. Mike about this and he said that there should not really be a problem with not punching the seats out for the speaker so i chose not to! i installed the one side today in the car to here what the speakers sounded like and i can not tell a difference with the leather seat covers on so now i have smooth looking seats and no holes in them also! hope this helps!<BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||1
